@page "/singularity-studios"
@layout BareLayout

<PageTitle>Singularity Studios // Sound, Stage & SFX</PageTitle>

<main class="studios-shell">
    <header class="studios-header">
        <a class="studios-back" href="/">← THE SINGULARITY WORKSHOP</a>
        <div class="studios-kicker">SINGULARITY CITY / CREATIVE INFRASTRUCTURE</div>
        <h1>Singularity <em>Studios</em></h1>
        <p class="studios-lede">Build the scene once. Reuse the world data. Shoot it, stage it, hear it, and inspect what made it happen.</p>
        <div class="studios-status"><span></span> STUDIO CONCEPT / WEBPAGE PROVING GROUND <i>·</i> NOT A PRODUCTION RENDER FARM</div>
    </header>

    <section class="studios-hero">
        <div class="studios-hero-copy">
            <div class="studios-index">01 / THE STAGE</div>
            <h2>A soundstage without a ceiling.</h2>
            <p>Singularity Studios is the Workshop's planned home for film, virtual production, choreography, and sound. Imagine indoor stages large enough for a full-scale sci-fi battle: sets, terrain, buildings, vehicles, performers, camera paths, motion rigs, lighting, and sound all describing one reusable scene.</p>
            <p>The aim is not to hand-build every shot from scratch. A stage becomes structured, versioned data that can be revisited, rearranged, rendered from another camera, or reused in another production.</p>
            <div class="studios-tags"><span>VIRTUAL PRODUCTION</span><span>CAMERA & RIGS</span><span>REUSABLE SET DATA</span><span>GIANT INDOOR STAGES</span></div>
            <a class="studios-data-link" href="/Workshop/Forge/StreamingAssets/Experiences/singularity-studios-stage.json" download>INSPECT / DOWNLOAD THE VERSIONED STAGE DATA ↗</a>
            <p class="studios-data-note">A small, explicit data fixture: one reusable set, two placements of the same prop definition, two cameras observing the same scene, and separate rig definitions. The giant-stage dimensions are illustrative planning targets—not verified runtime capacity.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="studios-stage-art">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 720 460" role="img" aria-labelledby="stage-title stage-desc">
                <title id="stage-title">Conceptual Singularity Studios soundstage</title>
                <desc id="stage-desc">A schematic indoor production stage with a central set, camera positions, a camera rail, lighting rigs, and sound coverage. This is a concept illustration, not a rendered production scene.</desc>
                <defs>
                    <pattern id="studio-grid" width="30" height="30" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M30 0H0V30" fill="none" stroke="#16404e" stroke-width="1"/></pattern>
                    <linearGradient id="studio-glow" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#00eaff" stop-opacity=".2"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#ff2cff" stop-opacity=".04"/></linearGradient>
                </defs>
                <rect width="720" height="460" fill="#030a14"/>
                <rect width="720" height="460" fill="url(#studio-grid)"/>
                <path d="M70 370 L360 205 L650 370 L360 430Z" fill="url(#studio-glow)" stroke="#1e6072"/>
                <path d="M70 100 L360 25 L650 100 L650 370 L360 430 L70 370Z" fill="none" stroke="#236074" stroke-width="2"/>
                <path d="M70 100L360 205L650 100M360 205V430M150 79V352M570 79V352M70 190L360 300L650 190" fill="none" stroke="#123848" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <g fill="#0b2636" stroke="#00eaff" stroke-width="1.5">
                    <path d="M265 295L365 238L455 286L355 344Z"/>
                    <path d="M265 295V220L365 164V238Z"/>
                    <path d="M365 238V164L455 212V286Z"/>
                    <path d="M295 278V237L328 218V259Z" fill="#123d4b"/>
                    <path d="M390 276V234L426 253V295Z" fill="#123d4b"/>
                </g>
                <g stroke="#ff2cff" stroke-width="2" fill="none">
                    <path d="M135 132H585M175 150H545"/>
                    <path d="M180 132V176M540 132V176"/>
                    <circle cx="180" cy="178" r="9"/><circle cx="540" cy="178" r="9"/>
                    <path d="M180 187L163 220H197Z" fill="#ff2cff" fill-opacity=".16"/>
                    <path d="M540 187L523 220H557Z" fill="#ff2cff" fill-opacity=".16"/>
                </g>
                <g fill="#00eaff" stroke="#00eaff">
                    <path d="M115 315L145 298L162 308L132 326Z"/><path d="M132 326V350L145 343V318Z"/><circle cx="137" cy="312" r="6"/>
                    <path d="M580 315L610 298L627 308L597 326Z"/><path d="M597 326V350L610 343V318Z"/><circle cx="602" cy="312" r="6"/>
                </g>
                <g fill="#d8fbff" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" letter-spacing="1">
                    <text x="92" y="58">LIGHTING TRUSS A</text><text x="458" y="58">LIGHTING TRUSS B</text>
                    <text x="78" y="285">CAM A</text><text x="570" y="285">CAM B</text>
                    <text x="270" y="390">REUSABLE SET / SCENE DATA</text><text x="280" y="448" fill="#00eaff">CONCEPT SCHEMATIC · NOT RENDER OUTPUT</text>
                </g>
            </svg>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="studios-grid" aria-label="Studio work areas">
        <article class="studio-card">
            <div class="studios-index">02 / PRODUCTION</div>
            <h2>Stage & camera</h2>
            <p>Block out the set, place cameras, define rails and rigs, choreograph performers, and preserve shot setups as reusable scene data.</p>
            <span class="studio-state">DIRECTION / NOT YET IMPLEMENTED</span>
        </article>
        <article class="studio-card">
            <div class="studios-index">03 / SOUND</div>
            <h2>SFX & sound design</h2>
            <p>Audition reference recordings, organize takes, and eventually author mixes. Creative sound is welcome—but it must be distinguished from sound claimed to emerge from a physical simulation.</p>
            <span class="studio-state">REFERENCE AUDIO AVAILABLE BELOW</span>
        </article>
        <article class="studio-card">
            <div class="studios-index">04 / PHYSICS</div>
            <h2>Hear the space</h2>
            <p>Follow source → space → listener. The target is to compare one source in an open field, a furnished room, a large hall, or behind a barrier using a declared acoustic model.</p>
            <span class="studio-state">FREE-FIELD OBSERVATIONS ONLY TODAY</span>
        </article>
    </section>

    <section class="studios-audio">
        <div class="studios-audio-copy">
            <div class="studios-index">05 / AUDIBLE PROOF OF PRESENTATION</div>
            <h2>Hear a reference source.</h2>
            <p>This browser sample proves only that the WebPage experience can present playable audio. It is a reference recording—not generated by the Physics solver, not a room simulation, and not a material-impact model.</p>
            <audio controls preload="none" src="https://interactive-examples.mdn.mozilla.net/media/cc0-audio/t-rex-roar.mp3">
                Your browser does not support inline audio. <a href="https://interactive-examples.mdn.mozilla.net/media/cc0-audio/t-rex-roar.mp3">Open the reference audio directly.</a>
            </audio>
            <a class="studios-audio-link" href="https://interactive-examples.mdn.mozilla.net/media/cc0-audio/t-rex-roar.mp3">OPEN REFERENCE AUDIO ↗</a>
            <small>Source: MDN interactive example, CC0 sample. External media availability is not controlled by this site.</small>
        </div>
        <div class="studios-acoustic-map">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 480 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="sound-title sound-desc">
                <title id="sound-title">Physical sound causality</title>
                <desc id="sound-desc">Conceptual flow from physical event through source coupling and space to listener observation. It is not an acoustic simulation result.</desc>
                <rect width="480" height="290" rx="10" fill="#040c17" stroke="#174151"/>
                <g font-family="monospace" text-anchor="middle">
                    <rect x="125" y="20" width="230" height="42" rx="5" fill="#0d2635" stroke="#00eaff"/>
                    <text x="240" y="46" font-size="12" fill="#e5fbff">PHYSICAL EVENT</text>
                    <path d="M240 62V87" stroke="#00eaff" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M234 81L240 88L246 81" fill="none" stroke="#00eaff" stroke-width="2"/>
                    <rect x="90" y="89" width="300" height="42" rx="5" fill="#24142c" stroke="#ff2cff"/>
                    <text x="240" y="115" font-size="12" fill="#ffe8ff">ACOUSTIC SOURCE MODEL</text>
                    <path d="M240 131V156" stroke="#ff2cff" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M234 150L240 157L246 150" fill="none" stroke="#ff2cff" stroke-width="2"/>
                    <rect x="125" y="158" width="230" height="42" rx="5" fill="#0d2635" stroke="#00eaff"/>
                    <text x="240" y="184" font-size="12" fill="#e5fbff">SPACE / PROPAGATION</text>
                    <path d="M240 200V225" stroke="#00eaff" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M234 219L240 226L246 219" fill="none" stroke="#00eaff" stroke-width="2"/>
                    <rect x="125" y="227" width="230" height="42" rx="5" fill="#14271c" stroke="#52e05a"/>
                    <text x="240" y="253" font-size="12" fill="#e8ffeb">LISTENER OBSERVATION</text>
                </g>
            </svg>
            <p>Conceptual causality map · not measured output</p>
        </div>
        <div class="studios-model-proof">
            <div class="studios-index">06 / EXECUTABLE PHYSICS EVIDENCE</div>
            <h2>Source-to-listener observation</h2>
            <p>This is the companion experiment's generated SVG, rendered from a serialized observation produced by <code>FreeFieldAcoustics.Observe</code>. It reports a 5 m path, estimated propagation delay, and free-field level—not an audio waveform.</p>
            <a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Physics/development/docs/experiments/acoustic-observation.svg">
                <img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Physics/development/docs/experiments/acoustic-observation.svg" alt="Generated free-field acoustic observation showing source and listener, five metre separation, propagation delay, and estimated received sound-pressure level" loading="lazy" />
            </a>
            <div class="studios-proof-links">
                <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Physics/blob/development/docs/experiments/acoustic-observation.md">EXPERIMENT & ASSUMPTIONS ↗</a>
                <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Physics/blob/development/docs/experiments/acoustic-observation.run.json">SERIALIZED RUN RECORD ↗</a>
            </div>
            <h3>Controlled distance sweep</h3>
            <p>Same source and reference level; only listener distance changes. This makes the current propagation rule inspectable before room acoustics are introduced.</p>
            <a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Physics/development/docs/experiments/acoustic-distance-sweep.svg">
                <img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Physics/development/docs/experiments/acoustic-distance-sweep.svg" alt="Generated acoustic distance sweep: estimated level falls from 80 dB SPL at one metre to 60 dB SPL at ten metres, with propagation delays increasing by distance" loading="lazy" />
            </a>
            <div class="studios-proof-links">
                <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Physics/blob/development/docs/experiments/acoustic-distance-sweep.md">DISTANCE SWEEP & ASSUMPTIONS ↗</a>
                <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Physics/blob/development/docs/experiments/acoustic-distance-sweep.run.json">SERIALIZED SWEEP RECORD ↗</a>
            </div>
            <small>Model output · the Physics CI is responsible for reproducing the JSON record and matching SVG. No room response or generated audio is claimed.</small>
        </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="studios-footer">
        <div><strong>THE STANDARD</strong><p>One scene model. Multiple cameras. Reusable assets. Honest evidence.</p></div>
        <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Physics/blob/development/docs/ACOUSTIC_WORLD_MODEL.md">READ PHYSICS ACOUSTICS ↗</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/WebPage/blob/development/docs/integrations/SINGULARITY_STUDIOS_SFX_WEBPAGELLM.md">INTEGRATION BRIEF ↗</a>
    </footer>
</main>

